<section class="wp-block-group alignfull ok-body"><!-- wp:group {"className":"ok-col","layout":{"type":"default"}} -->
<div class="wp-block-group ok-col"><!-- wp:heading {"level":2,"className":"ok-h2 ok-h2--left ok-col__h"} -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading ok-h2 ok-h2--left ok-col__h">Tuition and Core College Costs</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph {"className":"ok-copy"} -->
<p class="ok-copy">Okami College maintains a clear fee schedule for all programmes. Application and Saturday shift trial requires a one-time fee of €60. Tuition for the Two-year Diploma in Hotel Operations is €8,400 per year across two years, payable in term instalments. To secure an offered place, students submit a €900 place deposit within 21 days, which is deducted directly from year-one tuition. A one-time fee of €480 covers the professional uniform and knife kit, which remains yours to keep. Optional single residence rooms at Okami House cost €520 per month. Short courses include the ten-week Evening Certificate in Banquet Service at €1,250 and the two-day Front Desk Weekend Course at €390.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:heading {"level":2,"className":"ok-h2 ok-h2--left ok-col__h"} -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading ok-h2 ok-h2--left ok-col__h">Payment Schedule and Instalment Options</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph {"className":"ok-copy"} -->
<p class="ok-copy">Tuition for the two-year diploma is billed on a per-term basis to assist students and families with financial planning. Following acceptance, the €900 deposit confirms enrollment and is credited directly against the first term tuition invoice. The remaining balance for each academic year is split into two equal instalments due prior to the start of each eighteen-week term. Tuition includes all classroom instruction, floor mentoring at Okami House, operational materials, and placement supervision throughout the two years. Students living in the residence pay their €520 room fee monthly. We ensure that fee schedules are transparent from enrollment through graduation.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:heading {"level":2,"className":"ok-h2 ok-h2--left ok-col__h"} -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading ok-h2 ok-h2--left ok-col__h">Professional Equipment and Short Courses</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph {"className":"ok-copy"} -->
<p class="ok-copy">The €480 uniform and knife kit provides students with tailor-fitted service uniforms and professional kitchen knives required for floor shifts from the first week of Term 1. All uniform pieces and culinary tools are yours to keep after graduation. For hospitality professionals seeking specific credentials without enrolling in the two-year diploma, Okami College provides standalone options. The Evening Certificate in Banquet Service spans ten weeks for €1,250, while the intensive Front Desk Weekend Course delivers two days of reception and reservations training for €390. Both programmes share the teaching hotel facilities and expert faculty of Okami House.</p>
